=== DO THE PAIRED VARIANTS RETRIEVE THE SAME ADS? ===
   each pair differs ONLY in the language sentence — but one is written
   in Norwegian and the other in English, so this measures whether the
   lexical channel survives the language switch at all.

   pair     A title only   B + taxonomy
   p1               0/10           0/10
   p2               0/10           0/10
   p4               7/10           7/10
   p5               1/10           0/10

   mean  A 2.0/10    B 1.8/10    delta -0.2

   Arm A is the cross-language failure: `nurse` never matches `sykepleier`, so the
   English variant falls back to generic English vocabulary and retrieves chefs
   and bricklayers. Arm B indexes ad_taxonomy.job_title_en, populated for 100% of
   the corpus by A4's ESCO work, which bridges the two LEXICALLY — no encoder.

